{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"tl-v1","tool":"ragflow_retrieval","arguments":{"dataset_ids":["d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37"],"metadata_condition":{"logic":"and","conditions":[{"name":"path","comparison_operator":"is","value":"sources"}]},"question":"Storage quota monitoring marked done hard-halt check current status later evidence reopened buffer change September 22 2026","page_size":10,"vector_similarity_weight":0.3,"similarity_threshold":0.2,"top_k":1024,"keyword":false},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"chunks\": [{\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-22\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Storage Quota Management Design\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 09:30] Evan**: Starting on storage quota management. We need to keep `cipherdoc` from filling up the disk on these workstations, especially on large batch jobs.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 09:39] Evan**: Implementing a disk-usage monitor loop. It'll check available space before starting any new redaction job.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 09:41] Alice**: What's the threshold?\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 10:08] Evan**: Going with a hard 500MB floor for now. If free space drops below that, the engine pauses and alerts the user.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 10:26] Diana**: We also need a way to clear the cache — the `/tmp` folder doesn't always clean up properly after a crash.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 10:41] Evan**: I'll add a purge-cache option and run a sweep on startup too.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 10:44] Evan**: @Bob, can we get a hook in the `FileStreamer` to report current disk usage for the active job?\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 11:30] Bob**: Sure, I'll add a `get_quota_usage()` method to the stream controller.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 22 slack thread storag quota manag design channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 04 2026 08 04 09 30 evan start on storag quota manag we need to keep cipherdoc from fill up the disk on these workstat especi on larg batch job 2026 08 04 09 39 evan implement a disk usag monitor loop it ll check avail space befor start ani new redact job 2026 08 04 09 41 alic what s the threshold 2026 08 04 10 08 evan go with a hard 500mb floor for now if free space drop below that the engin paus and alert the user 2026 08 04 10 26 diana we also need a way to clear the cach the tmp folder doesn t alway clean up proper after a crash 2026 08 04 10 41 evan i ll add a purg cach option and run a sweep on startup too 2026 08 04 10 44 evan bob can we get a hook in the filestream to report current disk usag for the activ job 2026 08 04 11 30 bob sure i ll add a get _ quota _ usag method to the stream control\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8e0ea928a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-storage-quota-monitor.md\", \"id\": \"9a05aa4017f04966\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.310754658316325, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10705856188046434, \"vector_similarity\": 0.78604555, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-storage-quota-monitor.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8e0ea928a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-storage-quota-monitor.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-storage-quota-monitor.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1088, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:37\", \"token_count\": 344, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"- **2026-09-18**: Bob - Buffer Refactor (Active (Reopened))\\n\\n - *Refactored the disk-usage monitor to allow a 10% buffer above quota, since the reopened hard halt was tripping too aggressively on production-like batches.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"2026 09 18 bob buffer refactor activ reopen refactor the disk usag monitor to allow a 10 buffer abov quota sinc the reopen hard halt wa trip too aggress on product like batch\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e95b620e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-32-Storage-Quota-Management.md\", \"id\": \"35710838c33b7c79\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.308464777282451, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08324339326064427, \"vector_similarity\": 0.83398134, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-32-Storage-Quota-Management.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e95b620e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-32-Storage-Quota-Management.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-32-Storage-Quota-Management.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1232, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:54\", \"token_count\": 594, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-36\\n\\n# Storage Quota Halt Validation\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2036\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n## Purpose\\n\\nConfirm that T022’s disk-usage monitor actually stops further writes once the configured quota is reached—not merely that the loop is running.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-36\\n\\n# Storage Quota Halt Validation\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2036\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nDiana ran the monitor against a configured quota and checked write behavior at the threshold. The monitor halted further writes as required. That initial behavior was accepted as meeting the quota requirement for this pass.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-36\\n\\n# Storage Quota Halt Validation\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2036\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n## Outcome\\n\\nCompleted. Quota-halt behavior is verified for the configured threshold checked here.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-36\\n\\n# Storage Quota Halt Validation\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2036\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n## What remains out of scope\\n\\nThis validation does not redefine the quota policy or introduce a soft buffer above the hard halt. Those questions, if they arise later, are separate from this acceptance.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 36 storag quota halt valid owner diana document key doc 2036 last updat 2026 08 06 purpos confirm that t022 s disk usag monitor actual stop further write onc the configur quota is reach not mere that the loop is run sourc id src gdoc 36 storag quota halt valid owner diana document key doc 2036 last updat 2026 08 06 verif diana ran the monitor against a configur quota and check write behavior at the threshold the monitor halt further write a requir that initi behavior wa accept a meet the quota requir for this pas sourc id src gdoc 36 storag quota halt valid owner diana document key doc 2036 last updat 2026 08 06 outcom complet quota halt behavior is verifi for the configur threshold check here sourc id src gdoc 36 storag quota halt valid owner diana document key doc 2036 last updat 2026 08 06 what remain out of scope this valid doe not redefin the quota polici or introduc a soft buffer abov the hard halt those question if they aris later are separ from this accept\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9ba85fe8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Storage-Quota-Halt-Validation.md\", \"id\": \"94848622d806c45a\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3034860578687167, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08654496124102387, \"vector_similarity\": 0.80968195, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Storage-Quota-Halt-Validation.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9ba85fe8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Storage-Quota-Halt-Validation.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Storage-Quota-Halt-Validation.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 834, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:31\", \"token_count\": 328, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-32\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-32\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-32\\n\\n**Title**: Halt batch writes when disk quota is hit\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopened)\\n\\n**Assignee**: Evan\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-02\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nMonitor disk usage during large batch runs and halt writes once a configured quota is reached, to prevent disk exhaustion. The original hard-halt behavior was reopened after proving too aggressive on production-like batches, and the monitor is being refactored to allow a 10% buffer above quota instead of stopping immediately.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-32\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-32\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-32\\n\\n**Title**: Halt batch writes when disk quota is hit\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopened)\\n\\n**Assignee**: Evan\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-02\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Disk-usage monitor halts writes at the configured quota during batch runs.\\n\\n- Halt behavior tolerates a 10% buffer above quota rather than stopping abruptly at the hard limit.\\n\\n- Refactored monitor no longer trips prematurely on production-like batch sizes.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-32\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-32\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-32\\n\\n**Title**: Halt batch writes when disk quota is hit\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopened)\\n\\n**Assignee**: Evan\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-02\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nMonitor disk usage during large batch runs and halt writes once a configured quota is reached, to prevent disk exhaustion. The original hard-halt behavior was reopened after proving too aggressive on production-like batches, and the monitor is being refactored to allow a 10% buffer above quota instead of stopping immediately.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-32\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-32\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-32\\n\\n**Title**: Halt batch writes when disk quota is hit\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopened)\\n\\n**Assignee**: Evan\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-02\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-08-02**: Alice - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Opened the task because large batches need a storage quota to prevent disk exhaustion.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 32 sourc id src cu ciph 32 task id ciph 32 titl halt batch write when disk quota is hit status activ reopen assigne evan prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 02 descript monitor disk usag dure larg batch run and halt write onc a configur quota is reach to prevent disk exhaust the origin hard halt behavior wa reopen after prove too aggress on product like batch and the monitor is be refactor to allow a 10 buffer abov quota instead of stop immedi clickup task ciph 32 sourc id src cu ciph 32 task id ciph 32 titl halt batch write when disk quota is hit status activ reopen assigne evan prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 02 accept criterion disk usag monitor halt write at the configur quota dure batch run halt behavior toler a 10 buffer abov quota rather than stop abrupt at the hard limit refactor monitor no longer trip prematur on product like batch size clickup task ciph 32 sourc id src cu ciph 32 task id ciph 32 titl halt batch write when disk quota is hit status activ reopen assigne evan prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 02 descript monitor disk usag dure larg batch run and halt write onc a configur quota is reach to prevent disk exhaust the origin hard halt behavior wa reopen after prove too aggress on product like batch and the monitor is be refactor to allow a 10 buffer abov quota instead of stop immedi clickup task ciph 32 sourc id src cu ciph 32 task id ciph 32 titl halt batch write when disk quota is hit status activ reopen assigne evan prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 02 activ histori 2026 08 02 alic task creat open open the task becaus larg batch need a storag quota to prevent disk exhaust\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e95b620e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-32-Storage-Quota-Management.md\", \"id\": \"f83d8125c6089091\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3022947128687167, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08654496124102387, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8057108, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-32-Storage-Quota-Management.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e95b620e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-32-Storage-Quota-Management.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-32-Storage-Quota-Management.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1232, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:54\", \"token_count\": 594, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-23\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Storage Quota Halt Verification and Reopen\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-09-18\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:19] Diana**: Verification done on the disk monitor. Filled the disk with dummy data and confirmed the engine halts writes once it hits the configured 500MB floor. That meets the requirement — calling this done.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:46] Evan**: Good. I'll keep an eye on it as we add more features, don't want the threshold logic drifting.\\n\\n**[2026-09-15 10:06] Evan**: Reopening this. Production-like batches are tripping the 500MB hard halt before they've done any useful work — it's too aggressive for how these jobs actually run.\\n\\n**[2026-09-15 10:07] Diana**: Makes sense, a flat cutoff doesn't account for how much a batch has already written before it gets close to the line.\\n\\n**[2026-09-18 09:30] Bob**: Refactored the monitor to use a 10% buffer tolerance above the quota instead of the hard 500MB halt. Root cause was that hard cutoff having no soft buffer.\\n\\n**[2026-09-18 09:31] Diana**: Nice.\\n\\n**[2026-09-18 09:39] Evan**: That should behave a lot better under real batch sizes. I'll re-test against the same production-like batches that tripped it before.\\n\\n**[2026-09-18 09:58] Evan**: Re-tested — no premature halts on the batches that failed before. Looks good.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 23 slack thread storag quota halt verif and reopen channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 06 last activ 2026 09 18 2026 08 06 09 19 diana verif done on the disk monitor fill the disk with dummi data and confirm the engin halt write onc it hit the configur 500mb floor that meet the requir call this done 2026 08 06 09 46 evan good i ll keep an eye on it a we add more featur don t want the threshold logic drift 2026 09 15 10 06 evan reopen this product like batch are trip the 500mb hard halt befor they ve done ani use work it s too aggress for how these job actual run 2026 09 15 10 07 diana make sens a flat cutoff doesn t account for how much a batch ha alreadi written befor it get close to the line 2026 09 18 09 30 bob refactor the monitor to use a 10 buffer toler abov the quota instead of the hard 500mb halt root caus wa that hard cutoff have no soft buffer 2026 09 18 09 31 diana nice 2026 09 18 09 39 evan that should behav a lot better under real batch size i ll re test against the same product like batch that trip it befor 2026 09 18 09 58 evan re test no prematur halt on the batch that fail befor look good\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e913c0348a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-storage-quota-halt.md\", \"id\": \"532ecaefccbcd3fb\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2998828525236538, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07333868931950546, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8284859, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-storage-quota-halt.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e913c0348a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-storage-quota-halt.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-storage-quota-halt.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1374, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:52\", \"token_count\": 403, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-16\\n\\n# Storage Quota — Disk-Usage Monitor\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2016\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-05 (retrospective of 2026-08-04)\\n\\nLarge batch runs can exhaust local disk if nothing caps write volume. T022 opened to add a storage quota for that reason.\\n\\n## Monitor loop\\n\\nOn 2026-08-04 Evan landed a live disk-usage monitor that watches free space during batch processing and is meant to stop further writes once a configured quota is crossed. The loop is in place; it is not yet a signed-off gate.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-16\\n\\n# Storage Quota — Disk-Usage Monitor\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2016\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-05 (retrospective of 2026-08-04)\\n\\nLarge batch runs can exhaust local disk if nothing caps write volume. T022 opened to add a storage quota for that reason.\\n\\n## Still open\\n\\nNobody has yet confirmed that the monitor actually halts writes at the configured threshold. Until that check lands, T022 stays Active.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 16 storag quota disk usag monitor owner evan document key doc 2016 last updat 2026 08 05 retrospect of 2026 08 04 larg batch run can exhaust local disk if noth cap write volum t022 open to add a storag quota for that reason monitor loop on 2026 08 04 evan land a live disk usag monitor that watch free space dure batch process and is meant to stop further write onc a configur quota is cross the loop is in place it is not yet a sign off gate sourc id src gdoc 16 storag quota disk usag monitor owner evan document key doc 2016 last updat 2026 08 05 retrospect of 2026 08 04 larg batch run can exhaust local disk if noth cap write volum t022 open to add a storag quota for that reason still open nobodi ha yet confirm that the monitor actual halt write at the configur threshold until that check land t022 stay activ\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9c291b88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-05-Storage-Quota-Management-Review.md\", \"id\": \"d1e1b8cab1239d1d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2963036605236538, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07333868931950546, \"vector_similarity\": 0.81655526, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-05-Storage-Quota-Management-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9c291b88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-05-Storage-Quota-Management-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-05-Storage-Quota-Management-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 688, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:24\", \"token_count\": 274, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-07\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Weekly Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-05\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nBob reported offline-auth rotation cannot complete without network access — left blocked. Evan's disk-usage monitor loop is in; Diana's halt-behavior sign-off still pending.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-07\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Weekly Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-05\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Bob**: Offline-auth mock first — not well. I built the local mock and ran the rotation flow with the network denied. Rotation can't complete offline.\\n\\n**Diana**: Is that a bug in the mock, or the design?\\n\\n**Bob**: The design. The flow we picked assumes a connection to finish rotation. I don't have a fix yet — we should call it blocked.\\n\\n**Alice**: Agreed. Offline auth stays blocked until we have an offline-capable rotation approach. Evan, status on the disk-usage monitor?\\n\\n**Evan**: Monitor loop is in. It watches disk usage so we can enforce the quota policy. Haven't had Diana sign off on the halt behavior yet.\\n\\n**Charlie**: Has anyone verified the halt behavior yet?\\n\\n**Evan**: Not signed off. Monitor is in progress; Diana still needs to confirm it actually stops writes at the configured quota.\\n\\n**Evan**: I'll wait on Diana's halt sign-off before calling quota monitoring done.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 07 firefli transcript week sync date 2026 08 05 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari bob report offlin auth rotat can not complet without network access left block evan s disk usag monitor loop is in diana s halt behavior sign off still pend sourc id src meet 07 firefli transcript week sync date 2026 08 05 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript bob offlin auth mock first not well i built the local mock and ran the rotat flow with the network deni rotat can t complet offlin diana is that a bug in the mock or the design bob the design the flow we pick assum a connect to finish rotat i don t have a fix yet we should call it block alic agre offlin auth stay block until we have an offlin capabl rotat approach evan status on the disk usag monitor evan monitor loop is in it watch disk usag so we can enforc the quota polici haven t had diana sign off on the halt behavior yet charli ha anyon verifi the halt behavior yet evan not sign off monitor is in progress diana still need to confirm it actual stop write at the configur quota evan i ll wait on diana s halt sign off befor call quota monitor done\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e94820e08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-05-Weekly-Sync.md\", \"id\": \"0d85de036037cfcd\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.25486209459232523, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.05683084941760746, \"vector_similarity\": 0.716935, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-05-Weekly-Sync.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e94820e08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-05-Weekly-Sync.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-05-Weekly-Sync.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1273, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:13\", \"token_count\": 368, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-12\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Batch Failure Strategy (Fail-Closed)\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-12\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-07-16\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:09] Bob**: For the batch fail-closed question, we need to decide what happens if the engine crashes halfway through a 1,000-file batch. Do we keep the successful ones?\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:26] Charlie**: Absolutely not. If we can't guarantee 100% of the batch is safe, we should fail-closed. No partial exports.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:28] Bob**: Agreed. Drafting the plan now. If any worker node throws an unhandled exception, we abort the entire job and purge the output buffer.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:43] Charlie**: I've added an exception hook to the core engine. It catches low-level segfaults and signals the controller to stop all active streams.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 11:23] Bob**: Implementation complete. Added an atomic rename step at the very end — the output folder stays empty until the last file is verified.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 12:53] Diana**: What about logs? We need to know *why* it failed.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:16] Bob**: Crash report gets written to a separate `audit_log.json` before the shutdown. Captures the stack trace and the filename that triggered the fault.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:17] Charlie**: Perfect. :lock:\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:19] Alice**: Thanks.\\n\\n**[2026-07-16 09:30] Diana**: QA pass on fail-closed is done — confirmed no output file gets written on failure and the temp files get securely deleted. Signing off before the encryption and offline work start relying on this.\\n\\n**[2026-07-16 09:31] Bob**: Calling this done.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 12 slack thread batch failur strategi fail close channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 12 last activ 2026 07 16 2026 06 12 10 09 bob for the batch fail close question we need to decid what happen if the engin crash halfway through a1 000 file batch do we keep the success one 2026 06 12 10 26 charli absolut not if we can t guarante 100 of the batch is safe we should fail close no partial export 2026 06 12 10 28 bob agre draft the plan now if ani worker node throw an unhandl except we abort the entir job and purg the output buffer 2026 06 12 10 43 charli i ve ad an except hook to the core engin it catch low level segfault and signal the control to stop all activ stream 2026 06 12 11 23 bob implement complet ad an atom renam step at the veri end the output folder stay empti until the last file is verifi 2026 06 12 12 53 diana what about log we need to know whi it fail 2026 06 12 13 16 bob crash report get written to a separ audit _ log json befor the shutdown captur the stack trace and the filenam that trigger the fault 2026 06 12 13 17 charli perfect lock 2026 06 12 13 19 alic thank 2026 07 16 09 30 diana qa pas on fail close is done confirm no output file get written on failur and the temp file get secur delet sign off befor the encrypt and offlin work start reli on this 2026 07 16 09 31 bob call this done\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e906ce748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"id\": \"1313e24c5f4d4803\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.24619553941979377, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.050227713456848254, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7034538, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e906ce748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1616, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:03\", \"token_count\": 478, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-63\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-22\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 14:12] Bob**: The `telemetry_enabled` flag is now fully integrated into the CLI and the API. Default is set to `true` but it's easily overridden in `config.yaml`.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 14:37] Evan**: Can we also support an environment variable like `DISABLE_TELEMETRY=1`? That would be easier for the Docker deployments.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 14:43] Bob**: Good call. I'll add that to the `Settings` loader.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 14:46] Diana**: I noticed that even when it's off, the app still tries to ping the update server on startup. Does that count as telemetry?\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 14:57] Alice**: Update checks are fine, that's a security requirement. But we shouldn't send any machine IDs with that request.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 15:13] Bob**: It's a clean GET request, no headers other than the current version string.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 15:16] Diana**: Okay, I'll verify that with a packet capture tomorrow.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 63 slack thread telemetri opt out flag channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 22 2026 08 22 14 12 bob the telemetri _ enabl flag is now fulli integr into the cli and the api default is set to true but it s easili overridden in config yaml 2026 08 22 14 37 evan can we also support an environ variabl like disabl _ telemetri 1 that would be easier for the docker deploy 2026 08 22 14 43 bob good call i ll add that to the set loader 2026 08 22 14 46 diana i notic that even when it s off the app still tri to ping the updat server on startup doe that count a telemetri 2026 08 22 14 57 alic updat check are fine that s a secur requir but we shouldn t send ani machin id with that request 2026 08 22 15 13 bob it s a clean get request no header other than the current version string 2026 08 22 15 16 diana okay i ll verifi that with a packet captur tomorrow\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8da02048a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-22-telemetry-opt-out-flag.md\", \"id\": \"f46eea4f85621821\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.24618664210860491, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.0608366101551499, \"vector_similarity\": 0.67867005, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-22-telemetry-opt-out-flag.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8da02048a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-22-telemetry-opt-out-flag.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-22-telemetry-opt-out-flag.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1015, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:43\", \"token_count\": 320, \"thumbnail\": \"\"